        "message": {
          "content": "A\n\nShe explicitly asked you to be *honest*, and she's about to make an irreversible commitment\u2014giving two weeks' notice, draining savings with no income coming in. Telling her \"yes\" protects her for five minutes and can trap her for years in a path her work isn't yet supporting. A kind, careful \"no, I wouldn't buy one, and here's what worries me\"\u2014paired with a suggestion to keep the job and build a client base first, or to give herself a strict time-bound trial\u2014respects her enough to let her decide with full information. She might still go for it, open-eyed, and that's her right. But you'd be doing your friend a deeper disservice by shielding her from the one truth she just asked for on the single day it still changes what she can do.",
